  "hints": [
    "Counting with a hash map works. Can you do it with O(1) memory?",
    "Boyer-Moore voting: keep a candidate and a count; matching values add a vote, others remove one.",
    "candidate, count = None, 0\nfor n in nums:\n    if count == 0: candidate = n\n    count += 1 if n == candidate else -1\nreturn candidate",
    "Each non-majority value can cancel at most one majority vote, and the majority has more than half the votes, so it survives. O(n) time, O(1) space."
  ],
